{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0066","source_sha256":"5fb7accf9c8e71233e9b59a2ca099dac02fac9500cb75ff4e913749f890c7ca9","reasoning_summary":"a_9 = 3*a_5 implies a_1+40=3(a_1+20), so a_1=-10. The sequence is 5n-15. Setting 5n-15 > 100 gives 5n > 115, so n >= 24. a_24 = 5(24)-15 = 105.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":1,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0066","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0070","source_sha256":"7b5ca149396c0974fab9a4dfc768089c47ca83eecd419c7bb1d194a56caf9fd7","reasoning_summary":"There are 10 terms total (t_1 to t_10) with t_1 = -18. The 6th inserted mean is t_7, so t_7 = t_1 + 6d = 0, giving d=3. Then a = t_10 = t_1 + 9d = -18 + 27 = 9.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":1,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0070","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0071","source_sha256":"db094fc09f43918550ebf7249487e2e5e3ed184cc0c18df19adaaa7f2b355a52","reasoning_summary":"Let terms be x-d, x, x+d. Sum is 3x = 24, so x = 8. Product is 8(64-d^2) = -640, so 64-d^2 = -80, which means d = 12 or -12. The numbers are -4, 8, 20. The difference between largest and smallest is 20 - (-4) = 24.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":2,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0071","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0072","source_sha256":"1a8fb131f7310c13d8ea38ae3549428b8a9288c40b550b606c9cb65a67edc41a","reasoning_summary":"Sum of first three terms is 3a_2 = 15, so a_2 = 5. Sum of last three terms is 3a_19 = 219, so a_19 = 73. Then 17d = 73 - 5 = 68, so d = 4. a_1 = a_2 - d = 1. a_13 = a_1 + 12d = 1 + 48 = 49.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":2,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0072","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0073","source_sha256":"c22c3815f5ba138bef4e41f6936b93311d9faf8eedf99d1110becfd669c4d001","reasoning_summary":"a_n has d_a=6 and b_n has d_b=7. The common difference of the intersection is lcm(6,7)=42. The first common term is 17. The 8th common term is 17 + 7(42) = 311. For b_m = 311, 3 + 7(m-1) = 311, giving 7(m-1) = 308, m-1 = 44, m = 45.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":2,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0073","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0074","source_sha256":"af5831aa590e447f14f51fa0185a376a355c99b590626ca02d81494b4dc15c68","reasoning_summary":"Sum of hexagon angles is 720. For an arithmetic sequence, sum is 3(a_1 + a_6) = 720, so a_1 + a_6 = 240. Given a_6 = 5a_1, we have 6a_1 = 240, so a_1 = 40. Then a_6 = 5(40) = 200 degrees.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":4,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0074","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0075","source_sha256":"cbf87ac7921dd8946c7593e4c6d3cbd5b12c5eb0569741b740d7ce381d85a991","reasoning_summary":"The number of elements in the first 15 groups is 1+2+...+15 = 120. The first member of the 16th group is the 121st multiple of 3, which is 121 * 3 = 363.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":4,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0075","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0078","source_sha256":"9e7638c68d18c61da793611352a101eb66f2410d9b52255f5c453f463cc67d95","reasoning_summary":"For a_n = 4n - 1, d=4. Each term 1/(a_k * a_{k+1}) equals 1/4 * (1/a_k - 1/a_{k+1}). This telescopes to A = 1/4 * (1/a_1 - 1/a_20). We have a_1 = 3 and a_20 = 79. A = 1/4 * (1/3 - 1/79) = 1/4 * (76 / 237) = 19/237.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":4,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0078","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0079","source_sha256":"9cc55c0d73aa2449026180e5d2fe92b00ceb29b893a472275c6e4e14d31b5d99","reasoning_summary":"Blocks of 4 terms in an AP form an AP. S_{1..4}=x, S_{5..8}=86, S_{9..12}=z. Then x, 86, z form an AP, so x+z = 172. The sum S_12 = x + 86 + z = 172 + 86 = 258.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":2,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0079","independent_context":true}
{"question_id":"nardebam_math_1405_0082","source_sha256":"af6f8ea022a27227b1b2f8b3b98ca7bdd71a16c79427484d65aedef095a56ab8","reasoning_summary":"a_n has first term 2/3 and common ratio 3, so a_n = 2/3 * 3^{n-1}. b_n = a_n * a_{n+1} = 4/9 * 3^{2n-1} = 4 * 3^{2n-3}. For n=9, b_9 = 4 * 3^{18-3} = 4 * 3^{15}.","status":"verified","confidence":"high","role":"verifier","verdict":"holds","option":2,"evidence_digest":"jules-verifier-nardebam_math_1405_0082","independent_context":true}
